README done by FP probably around 2016 for CODE2
 
this version combines recent modification of FP on lspgf (to allow diagonal wind with variable values of lspgf),
some minor additions to firetec (intent, new ignition pattern),
- large scale pgf has been refactored :
  + mode 1= cste lspgf (previously mode 2), mode 2= unisotropic lspgf (limiting streak functionality, previously mode 3) , mode 3= smoothed unisotropic lspgf (limiting streak functionality, prviously mode 4)
  => Beyond the change in mode number, the main additional functionality is that mode 2 and 3 (unisotropic forcing) work with wind not aligned with the domain

  + izlspg = 0 => mass flow for lspgf computed on the whole domain; izlspg = 1 => mass flow for lspgf computed for heigh zu
  => the interest of this functionality is to be able to specify the wind speed at the given height (for example to match an experimental data) with cyclic wind runs. The limitation is that the forcing is done for all i,j, so that if your forest has a fuel break in the middle, you can not specify the value in the open. You can just specify the mean wind velocity at a given height but it is a progress. Subzone can be can be added later if required.
- the initial profile based on LAI can be computed on a sudomain of the whole domain (for example the forest zone if you have a forest/break/forest transition)

- a functionality to have an output format on a subdomain of the whole domain (like the comp.out one) : the interest is to be able to export at high frequency on a subdomain of interest to limit generation of huge files

- a windspeedupfactor parameter, to entail to do wind runs with a larger time step than fire runs (with iwindfield in and out).

- a new ignition patterns: two lines starting from a given point (for Fireflux experiment): mode of ignition number 6.



but especially
- optimized use of updated (get rid of unuseful ones)
-  new higrad "light"
- new advection scheme mpdata "light"
- new updated (correction of corner pieces and functionality for np+1 arrays with periodicity np...)
